  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "SCOPE: The question asks for the raw difference in conversion rates (email minus paid_search). The answer reports an adjusted effect after segment standardisation, which is a different estimand.",
    "GROUNDING: The reported effect of -0.134 and the evidence values (-0.189, -0.161, -0.069, -0.134) do not appear in any of the printed outputs. The only printed difference is +0.0698 (email higher).",
    "OVERREACH: The answer presents the adjusted estimate as a \"true effect\" (average treatment effect) despite the channel not being randomly assigned, implying causality from observational data.",
    "UNACKNOWLEDGED DATA PROBLEMS: The answer does not discuss the non‑random assignment of the email channel or any remaining confounding beyond customer segment, which limits causal interpretation."
  ]
}
